<title>USA: U.S. June leading indicators unchanged-Conf. Board.</title>
<headline>U.S. June leading indicators unchanged-Conf. Board.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Conference Board index of leading, coincident and lagging indicators (1992=100) and percent changes from previous months, seasonally adjusted. Indicators: Index-- June  May (Prev)  Apr (Prev)  Mar (Prev)  -Leading    103.8  Unch   0.3   0.3  -0.1  -0.1   0.2   0.2</p>
<p> -Coincident 116.0   0.3   0.2   0.2   0.3   0.3   0.3   0.2</p>
<p> -Lagging    105.3   0.2   0.1   0.2   0.3   0.1   0.2   0.3</p>
<p>Following are components of the index of leading indicators with net contributions to monthly changes.</p>
<p>    -			  June    May (Prev)   Apr (Prev)   Mar</p>
<p> Average Workweek	 -0.07  -0.03 -0.03   Unch  Unch   0.07</p>
<p> Initial Jobless Claims -0.08   0.06  0.06  -0.13 -0.13   Unch</p>
<p> Consumer Goods Orders   0.02  -0.01 -0.01   0.05  0.05  -0.03</p>
<p> Slower Deliveries	-0.02   0.06  0.06  -0.01 -0.01   0.07</p>
<p> Capital Goods Orders    0.04   0.01  0.01  -0.01 -0.01  -0.03</p>
<p> Building Permits	 -0.02  -0.01 -0.01  -0.01 -0.01   0.01</p>
<p> Stock Prices		0.10   0.18  0.18  -0.07 -0.07  -0.02</p>
<p> Money Supply		0.05   Unch  0.01   0.08  0.08   0.07</p>
<p> Treasury Yield Curve   -0.06  -0.03 -0.03   0.02  0.02   0.01</p>
<p> Consumer Expectations   0.03   0.05  0.05  -0.01 -0.01  -0.02</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected June leading indicators to rise 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
